WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.870
All right, so listen up. Republicans are going
to try or better said they are trying to steal

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.029
that Kentucky gubernatorial election that

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:13.690
they lost, which I told you about yesterday.
By the way, big interest in my story yesterday

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.330
about the big wins by Democrats on Tuesday
evening and a bunch of different state and

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.890
local elections. Usually the stories where
I talk about local and state elections and

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:26.489
the implications that they just don't do that
well. But I got dozens of emails from yesterday's

00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:30.829
close to 100,000 views on YouTube and just
like the first 12 hours. So this is a good

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:36.970
sign that people are engaged with the races
that are going on. So one of those races was

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.340
the Kentucky gubernatorial race in Kentucky,
a very red state, which Donald Trump won by

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:49.980
30 points over. Hillary Clinton in 2016 had
a Trump loving governor named Matt bell gubernatorial

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.989
candidate named Matt Bevin. A major democratic
victory has taken place with democratic challenger,

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:01.670
Andy Beshear, the attorney general of the
state, knocking out the incumbent Republican

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:02.670
governor.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.040
Now this is Kentucky. It's not a blue state.
It's not a purple state. And officially at

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:13.780
this point in time, it is a blue victory in
a very red state. By 5,189 votes for Andy

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.840
Bashir, the Republicans are going to fight
to the end to steal the election. And here's

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:24.170
how they're going to do it. First of all,
as as a mere formality, the governor has refused

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:29.370
to concede. Now again, as I've said before,
concessions don't really do anything. But

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:34.700
later on it can be pointed to, to try to build
the case that they from the beginning didn't

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.430
believe that they had actually lost. Okay.
Because of the small margin, they are going

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:45.251
to demand that the entire state be re canvased
as it's called, because of concerns that they

00:01:45.251 --> 00:01:50.031
are generally talking about regarding voting
irregularities. Now, the thing is, they're

00:01:50.031 --> 00:01:52.310
not telling us what those irregularities are.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:56.539
Uh, they say quote, we want the people of
Kentucky to have absolute confidence that

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:00.450
their votes were counted as they should have
been counted, but there is no indication about

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:06.399
why someone would suspect that their vote
was not counted. And there's also no specific

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:10.890
claims or evidence that have been presented
that anyone's votes were not counted, particularly

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:16.010
in a way that would have hurt the democratic
candidate, uh, or helped the democratic candidate

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.290
as counted, but would help the Republican
candidate if they had been counted the correct

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:24.800
way. But the whole point of all of this is
not even to get the re canvassing to change

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:32.540
the results because it is unlikely that re
canvasing would flip 5,189 votes, which is

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:38.629
the margin of victory. So what's the real
point here? The point is they want to escalate

00:02:38.629 --> 00:02:43.909
the entire process to the state legislature,
which is controlled by Republicans because

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:50.019
section 90 of the Kentucky constitution says,
quote, contested elections for governor and

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:57.120
Lieutenant governor shall be determined by
both houses of the general assembly according

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.330
to such regulations as may be established
by the law.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:07.830
So understand that all of this is premised
on supposedly voting irregularities which

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:12.739
were not reported on election day and which
the Republicans refused to actually give us

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:18.940
any examples of, Bernie is furious saying
quote, in a democracy, we can not allow politicians

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:24.640
to just overrule the election results, the
vote, the will of the voters must be respected.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:30.450
Now this is a very long shot, especially since
even if the state legislature does get to

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:35.629
decide, they still need to establish, establish
some fixed process for how it's all going

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:40.569
to be carried out. It's not just they pick
the winner and they pick the Republican, but

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:47.439
it is still a last ditch effort and they are
extraordinarily desperate and the most likely

00:03:47.439 --> 00:03:52.910
way I'm guessing that they would try to make
some kind of progress is to make some kind

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:58.540
of argument about the libertarian candidate
supposedly getting 2% of the votes and that's

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.110
larger than the margin of victory for the
Democrat.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:05.379
And they will probably try to say there is,
you know, there were, there were votes credited

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:10.409
to the libertarian that were met for the Republican
or whatever. I mean, none of this stuff makes

00:04:10.409 --> 00:04:14.849
any sense. I'm just thinking ahead to what
they're most likely to do. If it sounds absurd

00:04:14.849 --> 00:04:20.080
and ridiculous to you, it's because it is
absurd and ridiculous, but they don't care.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:26.230
The means always justify the ends if it keeps
a Democrat out of office, even if the Democrat

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.380
one, so we're going to be watching this one
very closely. There's a lot of coverage about

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:34.870
this one on common dreams, daily COEs and
a lot of other activists, lefty websites.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:41.520
It's on Bernie Sanders radar. So hopefully,
um, it will not lend itself to a situation

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.860
where Republicans can actually pull this off,
but they are furious. They see what Tuesday

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.780
night's election results potentially mean
for them in 2020 they see what it means to

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:57.660
start losing state houses and governors mansions
in red States across the country.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.490
Virginia turned totally blue. There were interesting
results in some parts of Pennsylvania that

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:06.350
are traditionally red that I did not get to
on Tuesday night, which a lot of people emailed

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:11.360
me about and are important and and we hopefully
will get a chance to talk about at some point

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:17.240
so they see what is going on. Whether they
attribute it to being damaged by Trump or

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:22.210
not. It depends on which Republicans you talk
to. Some of them do, some of them don't. But

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:27.300
this is potentially going to be a bloodbath
in 2020 but I don't want a single one of you

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:31.750
to hear me say that and believe that now you
can rest on your laurels and not have to work

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:37.440
our asses off for 2020 we could take the Senate
back. It's an uphill battle, but I outlined

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:43.280
how it could happen, but it's only if we really
work in all of those important States where

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.940
there are elections that could go from Republican
to Democrat.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.770
We could knock out Donald Trump, but it's
going to come down to actually getting out

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:54.270
